# Documentation Rules

- Follow **PRD → HLD → Tech Plan**: product requirements first, then architecture, then implementation specs. Use the cursor-project-docs skill and [documentation-standards.md](../../docs/standards/documentation-standards.md).
- **ContextStream (when available):** Before creating or editing docs, use ContextStream `search` to find related PRDs, ADRs, tech plans. After adding or updating a key doc, capture a short decision in ContextStream with path to the doc (e.g. "Added PRD-001" → `docs/product/...`).
- Keep each doc focused on one subject. Use `README.md` as the index in each subdirectory.
- **docs/product/** — PRDs (what and why). **docs/architecture/** — HLD and ADRs (how at system level). **docs/tech-plans/** — implementation specs (how at code level). **docs/design/** — component and integration design.
- When adding or changing docs, maintain traceability: HLD sections reference PRD requirements; tech plans reference HLD components. Use consistent cross-references (e.g. PRD-001, ADR-002).
- Do not duplicate content; link to the canonical doc. Do not populate `.cursor/docs/` with content that contradicts `docs/`.
- **Before pushing to remote:** Run local tests; at least 80% must pass (see [development guide](../../docs/guides/development.md#run-tests-before-push)).
